diff --git a/docs/FAST-PATHS.md b/docs/FAST-PATHS.md
--- a/docs/FAST-PATHS.md
+++ b/docs/FAST-PATHS.md
@@ -609,6 +609,17 @@
 Open differences from Metal that no note announces yet, and runtime costs still above the
 driver's. Each is open work.
 
+- **Dropped work detection needs device timestamps.** A command buffer whose timeline passed
+  but whose timestamps read unavailable fails as `GpuRecoveryVictim`, with zero GPU times,
+  counted by `WorkCounts::unrun_command_buffers`. Its queue continues. Host-derived timing
+  cannot detect this condition; this does not add a watchdog or prove detection of every
+  driver recovery.
+
+- **Driver compilation needs stack headroom.** Normal inline compilation requires at least
+  4 MiB remaining stack; compile pool and relay threads use 8 MiB stacks. The asking-thread
+  preference is still subject to that headroom check. During exit or a relay-thread creation
+  failure, the call falls back to the asking thread, so those paths have no stack guarantee.
+
 - **A GPU that stops with no loss from the driver fails its work later than Metal's watchdog
   would, and its `VkDevice` leaks** (`command_buffer/stall.rs`). Metal ends long work itself,
   with `MTLCommandBufferErrorTimeout` (code 2): about 5 s on an Apple M3 Max (2^29 threadgroups
